# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is git-ignored.

# --- limits (apply to both usecases) ---
SBX_MEMORY=4g
SBX_CPUS=2
# Wrapper fallback when unset here: 1024 (code), 2048 (pentest — nmap &
# parallel scanners fork many threads). A value set here always wins.
SBX_PIDS=1024

# --- OCI runtime ---
# krun (default) runs sandbox AND proxy as microVMs via KVM: own kernel,
# own /tmp, own page tables — a container escape lands in the VM's user
# namespace, not on the host kernel. Requires `dnf install crun-krun` and
# an accessible /dev/kvm. runsc (gVisor) is the alternative user-space
# kernel. crun (plain container, host kernel) is supported but explicit
# only — the wrapper never falls back to it silently. The wrapper fails
# hard at startup if the chosen runtime (or /dev/kvm for krun) is missing.
# SBX_RUNTIME=krun

# --- terminal locale ---
# Locale the sandbox runs under (injected as LANG). It must be a locale the
# image generated: nb_NO.UTF-8 (default — Norwegian keyboard å/ø/æ in
# interactive mode) or en_US.UTF-8. To use another, generate it in the image
# first (code/Dockerfile locale-gen step). A value set here always wins.
# SBX_LOCALE=nb_NO.UTF-8

# --- model backend ---
# The sandbox reuses the host's Claude Code model config, so there is nothing
# to duplicate here: same model, effort, context and key, with only the
# loopback base URL rewritten to host.containers.internal (the runtime's
# pasta host address). The port is parsed from the base URL and granted to
# the proxy as a trusted upstream automatically. To use the real Anthropic
# API, change the host config (or point SBX_CLAUDE_CONFIG elsewhere / unset
# it and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
# SBX_CLAUDE_CONFIG=$HOME/claude.sh

# --- network egress ---
# 1 = open egress (proxy logs everything but bypasses the allowlist),
# 0 = allowlist enforced. Wrapper defaults: code=1 (open), pentest=0.
# A value set here always wins over the wrapper default.
# SBX_OPEN_NETWORK=1
